Consider the following constraint satisfaction problem:

- Variables: {X<sub>1</sub>, X<sub>2</sub>, X<sub>3</sub>, X<sub>4</sub>}
- Domains: D<sub>1</sub> = D<sub>2</sub> = D<sub>3</sub> = D<sub>4</sub> = {1, 2, 3}
- Constraints: {X<sub>1</sub> ≠ X<sub>2</sub>, X<sub>1</sub> ≠ X<sub>3</sub>, X<sub>1</sub> ≠ X<sub>4</sub>, X<sub>2</sub> ≠ X<sub>4</sub> X<sub>3</sub> ≠ X<sub>4</sub>}

After making the assignment {X<sub>1</sub> = 1, X<sub>2</sub> = 2} and D<sub>1</sub> = {1}, D<sub>2</sub> = {2}, the AC-3 algorithm is applied initialised with all arcs in the queue, in both directions. What are the remaining domains after the AC-3 algorithm has completed?

