Consider the following 4-queens problem:

- Variables: {X<sub>1</sub>, X<sub>2</sub>, X<sub>3</sub>, X<sub>4</sub>}
- Domains: D<sub>1</sub> = D<sub>2</sub> = D<sub>3</sub> = D<sub>4</sub> = {1, 2, 3, 4}
- Constraints: alldiff(X<sub>1</sub>, X<sub>2</sub>, X<sub>3</sub>, X<sub>4</sub>) ∪ {|X<sub>i</sub> − X<sub>j</sub>| ≠ |i − j|} where i ≠ j and i, j ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4}

The initial assignment for the constraint satisfaction problem is {X<sub>1</sub> = 2, X<sub>2</sub> = 4, X<sub>3</sub> = 1, X<sub>4</sub> = 2}:

The min-conflicts local search algorithm will be used to find a solution to the problem.

<ul style="list-style:none;padding-left:0"><li><p>a) Which variable will be chosen in the first iteration of the algorithm?</p><p><strong>Select one alternative:</strong></p><ul><li>A. X<sub>1</sub></li><li>B. X<sub>2</sub></li><li>C. X<sub>3</sub></li><li>D. X<sub>4</sub></li><li>E. random</li></ul></li></ul>

<ul style="list-style:none;padding-left:0"><li><p>b) In the best-case scenario, how many iterations are needed by the algorithm to find a solution?</p><p><strong>Select one alternative</strong></p><ul><li>A. 2</li><li>B. 3</li><li>C. 4</li><li>D. 5 or more</li><li>E. 1</li><li>F. 0</li></ul></li></ul>
